              code system, A.J. Koning and D. Rochman,            1025 1451   63
              A.J. Koning and D. Rochman,                         1025 1451   64
              Nuclear Data Sheets 113 (2012) 2841.                1025 1451   65
          (2) TENDL: Complete Nuclear Data Library for            1025 1451   66
              Innovative Nuclear Science and Technology,          1025 1451   67
              A.J. Koning, D. Rochman, J.Ch Sublet, N. Dzysiuk,   1025 1451   68
              M. Fleming and S. van der Marck,                    1025 1451   69
              Nuclear Data Sheets 155 (2019) 1.                   1025 1451   70
                                                                  1025 1451   71
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           1025 1451   72
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.61, compiled on         1025 1451   73
       Jan 30 2025, 17:29:54 at Villigen   , Switzerland. The RRR 1025 1451   74
       expands from 0 to 2.898332E+6 eV. A total of               1025 1451   75
       3 l-values are used and 45 resonances. The resonance       1025 1451   76
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              1025 1451   77
       The TARES database for the measured resonances is          1025 1451   78
        ->  default up to 500000.000000 eV.                       1025 1451   79
       Above this energy, the ladder approach is used.            1025 1451   80
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       1025 1451   81
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          1025 1451   82
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     1025 1451   83
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    1025 1451   84
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  1025 1451   85
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   1025 1451   86
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          1025 1451   87
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       1025 1451   88
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    1025 1451   89
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       1025 1451   90
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         1025 1451   91
       The s-wave average level spacing is 1076730.000000 eV and  1025 1451   92
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.000101 1e-4.              1025 1451   93
                                                                  1025 1451   94
