***************************** T A L Y S **************************1025 1451  134
                                                                  1025 1451  135
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1025 1451  136
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1025 1451  137
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1025 1451  138
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1025 1451  139
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1025 1451  140
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1025 1451  141
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1025 1451  142
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1025 1451  143
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1025 1451  144
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1025 1451  145
stored in this data file:                                         1025 1451  146
                                                                  1025 1451  147
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1025 1451  148
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1025 1451  149
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1025 1451  150
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1025 1451  151
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1025 1451  152
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1025 1451  153
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1025 1451  154
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1025 1451  155
- Recoil data                                                     1025 1451  156
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1025 1451  157
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1025 1451  158
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1025 1451  159
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1025 1451  160
- Residual production cross sections                              1025 1451  161
                                                                  1025 1451  162
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1025 1451  163
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1025 1451  164
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1025 1451  165
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1025 1451  166
                                                                  1025 1451  167
